WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.103
Dates hold a lot of hidden information:

2
00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:07.050
the year, the month, the quarter, even the day of the week.

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:11.655
In this lesson, you will learn to extract each part from a date column,

4
00:00:11.655 --> 00:00:14.944
and to find the earliest and latest dates in seconds.

5
00:00:14.944 --> 00:00:16.260
Let's unpack some dates!

6
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.404
We are working with survey start and end times.

7
00:00:21.404 --> 00:00:25.320
Select the end column, and on the Transform tab, open Date.

8
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.660
Here I choose Year, and the column now shows only the year: twenty twenty two.

9
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.338
Next, Month.

10
00:00:33.338 --> 00:00:37.807
The same menu gives you the month number, and also Start of Month, End

11
00:00:37.807 --> 00:00:40.680
of Month, Days in Month, and Name of Month.

12
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:54.472
Quarter tells you which quarter each date falls in, from one to four.

13
00:00:54.472 --> 00:00:55.940
Perfect for quarterly reports.

14
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.314
The Date menu also has Week and Day options:

15
00:01:02.314 --> 00:01:06.960
day of week, day of year, start of week, end of week, and Name of Day.

16
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:26.075
Remember:

17
00:01:26.075 --> 00:01:29.448
on the Transform tab, these tools replace the column.

18
00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:35.820
If you still need the full date, use the same tools from the Add Column tab instead.

19
00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:01.200
Here I add Name of Day on the today column.

20
00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.350
Now every row shows Monday, Tuesday, and so on.

21
00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:07.500
Great for seeing which days your team collected data.

22
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.653
The Date menu can also find the Earliest and Latest date.

23
00:02:19.653 --> 00:02:21.090
Earliest returns one value:

24
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.246
the first date in the column.

25
00:02:23.246 --> 00:02:26.840
Here it is the eighteenth of February, twenty twenty two.

26
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.720
That single value replaced the table, so I delete the step to bring the table back.

27
00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:02.145
Finally, the Time menu works the same way for hours, minutes and seconds.

28
00:03:02.145 --> 00:03:04.880
We will explore it in the next lesson!

